        "raw": "<p>Hey, all!</p><p>Back when I was in college, I started a little group called the Wittenberg Role-Playing Guild. &nbsp;The Guild is now in its 13th year and is now holding its 12th consecutive convention: &nbsp;<a href=\"http://www4.wittenberg.edu/student_organizations/rpguild/conventions/wittcon/xii/\">WittCon XII--The Dirty Dozen!</a></p><p>If you&#39;re around the I-70 Corridor on March 28th, come spend the day gaming with us! &nbsp;Starting at 9am and running till midnight,&nbsp;there are tons of rpg sessions, as well as board games and card games (including SotM, GSF, and Tactics), a costume contest, and tons more. &nbsp;WittCon is known for featuring regional indie-game creators, including <em>Conjuring Seasons</em> by White Wizards Workshop,&nbsp;<em>Grisleigh End </em>by Jon Anderson,&nbsp;<em>Era of the Ninja</em> from Mythical Eras of War Games LLC, and the&nbsp;<em>Shuffling Horror</em> system by GameWick Games. &nbsp;I&#39;ll be running demo scenarios of&nbsp;<em>Cold Steel Wardens</em>, as well. &nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">$5 gets you into the convention, gets you access to events at the con, and buys you a pizza-and-pop dinner, courtesy of Beavercreek Pizza Dive. &nbsp;</span></p><p>If you&#39;d like more info, feel free to ask away or check the link here: &nbsp;<a href=\"http://www4.wittenberg.edu/student_organizations/rpguild/conventions/wittcon/xii/\">WittCon XII--The Dirty Dozen!</a></p>",
